.TH "ANIMATION.CURRENTTIME" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Animation.currentTime \- Animation: currentTime property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]Animation.currentTime\f[B]\f[R] property of the Web
Animations API returns and sets the current time value of the animation
in milliseconds, whether running or paused.
.PP
If the animation lacks a \f[CR]timeline\f[R], is inactive, or hasn\(cqt
been played yet, \f[CR]currentTime\f[R]\(cqs return value is
\f[CR]null\f[R].
.SH VALUE
A number representing the current time in milliseconds, or
\f[CR]null\f[R] to deactivate the animation.
.SH EXAMPLES
In the \c
.UR https://codepen.io/rachelnabors/pen/PNYGZQ?editors=0010
Drink Me/Eat Me game
.UE \c
, Alice\(cqs height is animated so it can go from small to large or
large to small.
At the start of the game, her height is set between the two extremes by
setting her animation\(cqs \f[CR]currentTime\f[R] to half her
\f[CR]KeyframeEffect\f[R]\(cqs duration:
.IP
.EX
aliceChange.currentTime = aliceChange.effect.timing.duration / 2;
.EE
.PP
A more generic means of seeking to the 50% mark of an animation would
be:
.IP
.EX
animation.currentTime =
  animation.effect.getComputedTiming().delay +
  animation.effect.getComputedTiming().activeDuration / 2;
.EE
.SH REDUCED TIME PRECISION
To offer protection against timing attacks and fingerprinting, the
precision of \f[CR]animation.currentTime\f[R] may be reduced depending
on browser settings.
.PP
The value of this property can come from two sources: supplied by
script, or calculated from \f[CR]AnimationTimeline.currentTime\f[R],
\f[CR]startTime\f[R], and \f[CR]playbackRate\f[R].
The timeline\(cqs underlying clock can already be rounded before
calculation; see the timeline\(cqs reduced time precision for its
rounding intervals.
.PP
In Chrome, the browser does not apply additional timer rounding.
In Safari, the browser rounds the returned value to 0.001 ms, the
resolution used to represent animation times.
.PP
In Firefox, the browser rounds the returned value to 0.02 ms by default,
including in cross\-origin\-isolated contexts.
If \f[CR]privacy.resistFingerprinting\f[R] is enabled, the rounding
interval is 16.667 ms or the interval configured by
\f[CR]privacy.resistFingerprinting.reduceTimerPrecision.microseconds\f[R],
whichever is larger.
.PP
For example, these are possible values in Firefox:
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Reduced time precision (0.02 ms) with default settings\f[R]
animation.currentTime;
\f[I]// Might be:\f[R]
\f[I]// 23.4\f[R]
\f[I]// 24.18\f[R]
\f[I]// 25.5\f[R]
\f[I]// \&...\f[R]

\f[I]// Reduced time precision with \(gaprivacy.resistFingerprinting\(ga enabled\f[R]
animation.currentTime;
\f[I]// Might be:\f[R]
\f[I]// 50.001\f[R]
\f[I]// 66.668\f[R]
\f[I]// 83.335\f[R]
\f[I]// \&...\f[R]
.EE
